{"name":"get_client","title":"Get Client","description":"Get details for a single client.

Returns the upstream client object verbatim, exactly as the API answers it.

Example call (get_client):
    {
      "host": "my-console",
      "site": "Default",
      "client_id": "3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6"
    }","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"host":{"type":"string","description":"Console name (case-insensitive reportedState.hostname/name, e.g. "my-console") or data[].id (MAC:numericId), from list_hosts. Serves Network and Protect."},"site":{"type":"string","description":"Network site name or UUID; resolved server-side. Get it from list_local_sites
(name or id). Names like "Default" work."},"client_id":{"type":"string","description":"Connected client UUID or MAC (AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF, aa-bb-..., AABBCCDDEEFF);
a MAC is resolved to the client id with list_clients (macAddress filter), so the
client must be connected; an unknown MAC fails listing the connected clients.
Get it from list_clients (data[].id or data[].macAddress). Network-app id — not
a Protect id."}},"required":["host","site","client_id"],"type":"object"},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true},"_meta":{"unifi/apiSource":"network/official/read","fastmcp":{"tags":[]}}}
